Persist supervisor action continuity

Supervisor check-ins lost the last committed action when a parent session
unloaded because the context lived only in process memory.

Store the action and its timestamp in Saffron's auxiliary database. Scope
persisted state to the goal, clear it when the goal changes or ends, and
restore it at the existing continuity boundary. Preserve snooze delay and
reason, a bounded copy of a delivered follow-up, and aggregate snooze count
and duration so a reconstructed supervisor can evaluate the preceding action
without retaining private reasoning or an unbounded transcript.
